# **name**

Independent Nest 12/Bun application. The `hybrid` preset supplies operational HTTP
and GraphQL adapters, a recovering RabbitMQ consumer, composition and an explicit
message-handler port. Add business behavior under `application/` and `domain/`
only when needed. No User/Wallet implementation, CRUD or example assertions are copied.
The private package exports no application implementation.

## Run

From the workspace root, supply your own broker and an available HTTP port:

```sh
__PREFIX___HTTP_PORT=3010 __PREFIX___RABBITMQ_URL=amqp://localhost:5672 \
  bun run nx run __name__:serve
```

Use `__name__:watch` or `__name__:debug` for Bun watch/inspector mode. No dotenv
file is loaded. The only required variables are `__PREFIX___HTTP_PORT` and
`__PREFIX___RABBITMQ_URL`; `__PREFIX___RABBITMQ_QUEUE` defaults to
`__name__.commands.v1`. Configure broker heartbeat in the URL when needed.
Use a unique broker/queue per environment. The app does not prepare or delete
infrastructure and needs no sibling service or database.

HTTP starts while RabbitMQ is unavailable. `/health/live`, `/health/ready`,
`/health/ready/http`, `/health/ready/consumer`, `/health/ready/publisher` and
`/health/backlog` use the shared operational contract. Publisher and backlog are
not applicable until implemented. POST `{ "query": "{ httpReady }" }` to `/graphql`
for HTTP readiness. Broker retries use bounded exponential delays.

## Extend

Register message handlers in `composition/app.module.ts`. Each AMQP message uses
a JSON `{ "pattern": "your.versioned.pattern", "data": ... }` envelope and nonempty
AMQP `messageId` and `correlationId` properties. The adapter passes those identities
explicitly to the handler. Resolve `undefined` after committing effects. Return
`{ accepted: false, reason: 'invalid-your-payload' }` for permanent validation
rejections before effects; use a stable, non-sensitive reason code. Throw for
transient failures that should be retried.

Invalid envelopes and rejected payloads are retained byte-for-byte in
`<queue>.failed`, with publisher confirmation before ACK. Available identities,
content metadata and headers are preserved independently; `x-failure-reason`
records `invalid-json`, `invalid-envelope`, `missing-identity`, `unknown-pattern`
or the handler's rejection reason. Original expiration is omitted so inspection
evidence survives. The retention log includes the same reason and identities.

The 10-second handling deadline ends the AMQP session without acknowledging
uncertain work. It cannot cancel application effects: the transport waits for
the actual operation to settle before reconnecting or completing `stop()`.
A stuck handler keeps this instance unavailable until it settles or the process
is restarted. Other instances can receive redelivery after connection loss;
commit idempotency claims and effects atomically in the owning database before
resolving. This scaffold does not implement a business publisher or an outbox.

Use explicit `@Inject(Token)`, factory `inject` lists, GraphQL type functions and
explicit validation when adding adapters; Bun does not emit design metadata.
SIGINT/SIGTERM refuses new work, cancels deliveries, drains accepted work and closes
AMQP before Nest. The shared shutdown deadline is 15 seconds; timeout exits nonzero.

## Check and distribute

```sh
bun run nx run __name__:lint
bun run nx run __name__:typecheck
bun run lint:boundaries
bun run nx run __name__:test
bun run nx run __name__:test-component
bun run nx run __name__:distribution
```

Unit tests use `tests/unit/` without preload or infrastructure. Live tests use
`tests/component/` in an uncached target; their fixtures must own their resources
and cleanup. Neither directory contains generated tests, so each test command
reports no tests and exits nonzero until meaningful tests are added.

Copy `dist/__name__/` outside the workspace and run `bun run start` there with
the same environment. The artifact includes Bun TypeScript sources and its installed
runtime dependencies; no workspace or install is needed. Build for the deployment
OS/architecture using the pinned Bun version.

No database configuration or migration commands are generated. When adding persistence,
register only this application in `database/applications.ts`, add its own environment
prefix, runtime role and owned migrations, and use `DATABASE_APP=__name__` for workspace
migration commands. Add the migration tooling to `distribution.json`; the shared
packager includes scoped migration commands only for registered database applications.
Follow `docs/adding-an-application.md` in the workspace for the database/environment checklist.
